attribution: German folk song; the words circulated on broadsheets around 1780, the melody dates from about 1810-1820 and both were printed together in Hoffmann von Fallersleben and Ernst Richter's "Schlesische Volkslieder" (1842). Anonymous and public domain. Two verses.
source_url: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Die_Gedanken_sind_frei
tags: germany, freedom, folk, protest

